  "body": "The only failed expectation is proposal 798f9c99dc99cb9a. The proposer misread the rule. The rule documents the kernel as `conformance.kernel.grounding`, not as the internal function `_grounding_kernel`. The proposal's commitment line `\"kernel\": \"open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle._grounding_kernel\"` names a function that is not a registered kernel, so the execution returned `MINI_OPEN_KERNEL_NOT_FOUND: 'oracle' has no '_grounding_kernel'`. The rule's words are: \"conformance.kernel.grounding: The harness's grounding verdict for a value, its cited span and the document, no relaxation, value-in-span checked: the input is one JSON object {\"value\", \"span\", \"document\"}; GROUNDED, SPAN_MISSING, SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT or VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN.\" The proposer should build next a pair that uses the documented kernel name `conformance.kernel.grounding` (or the correct identifier from the kernel registry) instead of the internal function name.",
